Where it went:
  src/{earcut,extrude,frames,lathe,merge,path2,polyhedron,shape,sweep,trig}.rs
                         -> crates/shape-gen/src/
  src/lib.rs (Mesh, Placement, place, ...)  -> crates/shape-gen/src/lib.rs
  src/lib.rs (mod geom_contracts)           -> crates/shape-bool/tests/og_geom_contracts.rs
  src/{csg,fracture}.rs  -> crates/shape-bool/src/

Changes from the source:
  - og_core::sort -> shape_core::sort (std's stable sort: same order).
  - csg.rs, fracture.rs: HashMap/HashSet -> BTreeMap/BTreeSet (lookups
    only; keys are sorted before any iteration, so output is unchanged).
    Origin derives Ord.
  - finish, vertex_normals, normalize, Placed, place: pub(crate) -> pub
    (#[doc(hidden)]), so shape-bool can use them.
  - trig.rs tests check the series against libm (shape_core::trig), not
    std. og-geom's series trig itself is kept, so generator output
    matches the engine and its TypeScript twin bit for bit.
  - csg.rs: csg_traced split into arrange() (steps 1-3 and the keep
    decision) and its emission, unchanged in output; csg_points() added,
    an f64 entry on welded operands that refuses open operands.
